// FRAGMAR  24x24 x2  (144 B)  <- tools/sprites/fragmar.txt
// FRAGMAR - species 2, family 1 stage 1, type SIGNAL (PACKET / BALANCED).
// 'It splits itself apart to slip through.'
// root:       capsule - rounded rect with a solid header stripe
// silhouette: the capsule torn into three shards along an 18px line, 2px gaps,
// zigzag tear edges, one eye on the lead shard.
// frame 2:    the three shards scissor 1px apart and snap back.
// Family motif: a rounded-rect body cut by an unlit HEADER SEAM, eye holes in the header field, stub feet. All three stages are the same rect: whole, torn, then shattered.
// PAKETO's rect, 20px wide now, cut by two 3px zigzag tear channels. The LEAD
// shard keeps the eye and both feet, so the outer two can scissor without the
// legs coming off the floor. Frame 0 is the shards 1px apart; frame 1 is the
// snap back.
// THE THIRD SHARD IS A SHARD NOW (P9-C6). It was a 3px dash at the frame edge
